<<~ ahu slot=`#/unfinished-threads-and-present-carriers`>>

!! Unfinished threads and present carriers

- ''REACHED:'' Chapter 06 still carries many pending power conversions (194 matching pending/review lines in the span), a `Finger of Death` review case recorded by the tracker, and open alpha checks for tag/Overcharge consistency, recognizer discoverability, and Level versus Power Level. ''INFERRED:'' each converted Power would live in `bags/sdm/ha.ka.ba/sdm/modules/powers/`, with its source account under `witness/powers/osr-spells/` and FTLS view under `projections/powers/ftls-card/`; `templates/modules/power.mem` and `templates/projections/powers/ftls-card.mem` supply the current shapes. The chapter and `_osr/FTLS/TODO_FTLS_Chapter_Action_Plan.md` retain the full backlog.
- ''REACHED:'' Chapter 06's locked Overcharge/rank-tag, ritual, and ECM material includes placeholders; the current epic explicitly leaves lock state, rank tags, interaction doctrine, and hard cases open while Sprints 0–3 stand complete and further Power work remains deferred. ''INFERRED:'' shared doctrine belongs with `bags/sdm/ha.ka.ba/sdm/epic/powers-composition-rewrite.mem` and `docs/composition-model.mem`; particular implementations belong with component, module, mount-point, and witness memes. This names the carriers without deciding the design.
- ''REACHED:'' The FTLS action tracker leaves Chapter 02 Paths, 03 Heritage, 04 RSS additions, 07 danger/corruption, 08 conflict, 09 loot procedure, 10 referee aids, and cross-chapter checks unchecked. The Chapter 05 item bridge and `_osr/FTLS/TODO_Loot_Treasure_Conversion.md` also remain open. ''INFERRED:'' their detailed book prose still lands in `ftls/`; when one becomes an addressed SDM pattern, `bags/sdm/ha.ka.ba/sdm/` supplies the corresponding carrier. The powers epic does not absorb these whole chapters.
- ''REACHED:'' `_osr/FTLS/TODO_SDM_Powers_Index.md` records completed scans of five named sources but still asks whether other sources require a scan. ''INFERRED:'' that question remains in the source QA record until the operator settles its scope; individual source attestations fit the `bags/sdm/ha.ka.ba/sdm/witness/` pattern.
<<~/ahu>>

